+| `lan2.sh` | Two `live.sh`-style runs on one PC for LAN play (`MKW_LAN=1`), each in its own network namespace inside a user namespace (no root), joined by a veth pair: A at 10.77.0.1, B at 10.77.0.2, B with its profile copy `build/profile-b`; one job unit caps the pair (`JOB_MEM`, 14G) | `tools/run/lan2.sh NAME [SECONDS]`, then `ctl.sh NAME-a`/`NAME-b ...`, `ctl.sh NAME stop` |
+| `ctl.sh` | Sends a command to that run and waits for its answer: `frame`, `shot PATH` (whole screenshot and `PATH-s.png` 1280 wide for viewing), `dump DIR [ubo|lut]` (dump of the next frame), `flight`, `mem ADDR SIZE PATH` (game memory to a file), `tex ADDR` (textures over that address; 0: pool images larger than their storage), `press <ticks> <button> [hold]`, `stop` | `tools/run/ctl.sh NAME COMMAND...` |
+| `vpad.py` | A virtual Xbox 360 pad (Linux uinput) that plays a list of presses: the overlay menu reads the real pad, not `ctl.sh press`. The run needs `SDL_JOYSTICK_ALLOW_BACKGROUND_EVENTS=1` (its window has no focus) | `uv run tools/run/vpad.py back+start:600 wait:800 right` |
+| `at.sh` | `ctl.sh` commands when the game enters one of its phases (`AIGlobalSeq*` nodes: `TitleMenuMain`, `PartsSelectEx`, `SimpleConfirm`, `ReadyRace`, `WaitIntroMovie`…), not at a frame number. The run needs `MKW_SEQ_WATCH=1`; `MKW_SEQ_HOLD=WaitIntroMovie` lets the movie play without the script skipping it | `tools/run/at.sh NAME PHASE [+FRAMES] command [arg] [-- command...]` |
+| `flicker.sh` | Counts the frames with a black lower half in the 600 thumbnails up to a frame of a live run (title scene flicker) | `tools/run/flicker.sh NAME [FRAME]` |
+| `press-split2.txt` | Presses for a two-player split-screen race, by game phase: with `MKW_VIRTUAL_PADS=2` and `MKW_SEQ_WATCH=1` as `MKW_INPUT_SCRIPT` | `MKW_VIRTUAL_PADS=2 MKW_INPUT_SCRIPT=tools/run/press-split2.txt tools/run/race.sh NAME` |
+| `press-split4.txt` | The same for four players (`MKW_VIRTUAL_PADS=4`) | `MKW_VIRTUAL_PADS=4 MKW_INPUT_SCRIPT=tools/run/press-split4.txt tools/run/race.sh NAME` |
+| `race.sh`, `press-race.txt` | A run up to the race: A every 90 frames from frame 700, 720p overlay (`build/romfs-res`, made by `tools/romfs/resolution.py`; without it a 1.8.0 race renders at 2560x1440), BC1 off; calls `run_perf.sh`. Exits by itself 20 s (`RACE_SECS`) after the race starts, with phase watching off from there and the `MKW_HOST_TIME` census of that window | `tools/run/race.sh NAME [SECONDS]` |
+| `race.sh RACE_TT=1` | Up to a time trial with `MKW_QUICK_RACE=tt` (phase script in `runtime/input/input.c`) (Mario, standard kart, Cheep Cheep Falls, solo): a grid with a single kart 29.6 s after boot. With `MKW_UI_FOCUS=1` the log says which button has the cursor (`ui: focus L_Btn_02`) | `RACE_TT=1 tools/run/race.sh NAME` |
+| `race.sh RACE_GP=1` | Up to a Grand Prix with `MKW_QUICK_RACE=gp` (phase script in `runtime/input/input_script.c`): the first entry everywhere (the character, kart and cup the save had last: not a fixed course), 24 karts, the course's flyover skipped. The kart drives with Smart Steering and Auto-Accelerate on in the save (the game's options; a time trial does not allow them), else A is held | `RACE_GP=1 tools/run/race.sh NAME` |
+| `ab.py` | A/B inside a run: with `MKW_AB=<s>` blocks A and B alternate (A B B A; B A A B with `MKW_AB_INVERT=1`) from the race start, and a switch `MKW_<X>=ab` only acts in the B blocks; compares the 60-frame windows that are entirely A or entirely B and, with normal and inverted runs, gives the change with the scene balanced. Between two identical runs there is up to 12 ms per frame of noise | `uv run tools/run/ab.py build/run/NAME.log` |
+| `run_perf.sh` | `build/mkw` (or another executable with `MKW_RUN_BIN`, e.g. a player folder's) under `perf record` (flat) with a GPU memory cap (4096 MiB, for the 660M: on a 12 GB discrete card it made races 59 ms a frame against 39-43 without it, in two runs with the GPU at its lowest clock, before `MKW_GPU_CLOCKS`; `MKW_GPU_MEM_LIMIT=0` for a player's numbers), and the 40 hottest symbols; `PERF_ARGS="-e cpu_core/cycles/u,cpu_atom/cycles/u --call-graph fp --user-callchains"` with a `build.py --frame-pointers` runtime gives call graphs under `perf_event_paranoid` 2 on a hybrid Intel CPU; opens the control FIFO like `live.sh` (`ctl.sh` and `at.sh` work with `race.sh` too) | `tools/run/run_perf.sh NAME [SECONDS]` |
+| `texms.sh` | Total render thread time in texture uploads (and ASTC) up to a frame, from a run's `perf` lines, and the worst frame | `tools/run/texms.sh build/run/NAME.log [FRAME]` |
+| `perf_split.sh` | Splits a profile by owner (game code, runtime, drivers) and lists the 15 hottest game functions | `tools/run/perf_split.sh FILE.perf` |
+| `kstacks.py` | Where each thread sleeps inside the kernel (stacks of `perf record -e cs -g` with kallsyms names) and the `mmap_lock` waits per thread and call | see its header (kallsyms needs root) |
+| `crit_path.py` | Critical path of each frame of an `MKW_CRIT` recording (with `MKW_TRACE=sched`): which thread and which state (running, waiting for a core, host call, wakeup latency) takes each ms between two presents (from totk-pc-recomp, MIT) | `uv run tools/run/crit_path.py FILE.bin` |
+| `rqwait.py` | With a run going, CPU and run-queue wait (ready without a CPU) of each `build/mkw` thread over a window of the race, by thread name (`/proc/.../schedstat`): whether a change takes host CPU away from the replay or the render | `uv run tools/run/rqwait.py build/run/NAME.log [--skip 6] [--secs 12]` |
+| `locks.py` | Wait on each runtime lock during the race, in ms per second, per lock, per requester and per holder while another waited (`MKW_LOCK_PROF=1`), with `build/mkw`'s names | `uv run tools/run/locks.py build/run/NAME.log` (Windows: `--exe build/dist/windows/mkw.exe`) |
+| `perf_sdk.py` | How much CPU the recompiled SDK code takes in a profile, per thread and per namespace (`nn::os`, libc, math…), with `build/bindb.sqlite`'s names | `uv run tools/run/perf_sdk.py scratchpad/NAME.perf` |
+| `sample_stacks.sh` | Stack snapshots through gdb when `perf` does not record call graphs (`MKW_ALLOW_PTRACE=1`) | `tools/run/sample_stacks.sh DIR [N] [GAP]` |
+| `gpu_ok.sh` | Refuses when amdgpu logged since boot a failed ring reset or a full GPU reset (after a failed reset, the next replay froze the machine); episodes recovered in the ring, however many, let it go on. Called by `live.sh`, `run_perf.sh` and `replay.sh`, which set `MKW_GPU_GUARD=1` | `gpu_ok.sh` |
+| `avail.sh` | MB available for a run: `MemAvailable` plus `GPUReclaim` (TTM page pool the kernel releases under pressure); used by the thresholds of `live.sh`, `run_perf.sh` and `replay.sh`; `--wait FLOOR` waits up to `WAIT_MEM` minutes for it | `avail.sh`, `WAIT_MEM=30 tools/run/race.sh NAME` |
+| `memwatch.sh`, `memtop.sh` | RSS, swap, GTT and VRAM every 5 s; memory maps with their Rss after N seconds | `memwatch.sh OUT.tsv`, `memtop.sh AT OUT` |
+| `stacks.py` | Stacks of every thread of a running `build/mkw`, with the game's names | see its header |
+| `summary.py` | A log summed up in ~15 lines: how it ended, last frame and phases, median and p95 frame time before and during the race, VRAM peak, `MKW_HOST_TIME` census, grouped failures and the game speed (a warning when the race runs in slow motion) | `uv run tools/run/summary.py build/run/NAME.log [...]` |
+| `gpucmp.py` | The race's GPU time of several runs side by side: median `gpu avg` and interval per 60-frame window in the race, whole `MKW_PASS_TIMING=1` windows in the race (busy and the largest pass) and the last texture memory; for changes without an in-run switch (`MKW_ASTC_BC1`) | `uv run tools/run/gpucmp.py build/run/NAME.log [...]` |
+| `why.sh` | Sourced by `run_perf.sh` and `live.sh`: under Claude Code (`CLAUDECODE=1`) a run without `MKW_RUN_WHY` (what I expect to see and what I conclude from each result) is refused and the captures of `build/cap` are suggested; each reason goes to `build/run/why.log` | `MKW_RUN_WHY="…" tools/run/race.sh NAME` |
+| `kwin-rule.sh` | KWin rule for our runs' windows (app id `mkw-recomp-run`, `MKW_BACKGROUND_WINDOW=1`): they never take the focus and open below the others; the player's window is not touched | `tools/run/kwin-rule.sh [--remove]` |
+| `wine.sh` | An `.exe` (`build/mkw.exe`, a self-test) in Wine with its own prefix in `build/win/wineprefix`, without Mono or Gecko: it shows no dialogs and does not touch `~/.wine`. Its `Desktop` is your desktop folder (Wine links it in every new prefix): what a test creates on the desktop (a `.lnk`) is deleted by hand | `tools/run/wine.sh PROGRAM.exe [ARGS...]` |
+| `envs.py` | Catalogue of the `MKW_*` variables the runtime reads (`cfg_get` and `rt_knob`): where and their comment, taken from the code | `uv run tools/run/envs.py [REGEX]` |
+| `sym.py` | Names the `build/mkw` addresses of the log (`exe+`, `mkw+`, base 0x200000) and, for translated code, its game function | `uv run tools/run/sym.py DIR...` or `< build/run/NAME.log` |
diff --git a/tools/run/host_server.py b/tools/run/host_server.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..29e7f45
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/run/host_server.py
@@ -0,0 +1,96 @@
+"""Configure this user's standalone lobby and coturn services without changing other applications.
+
+Why: players share one Linux service; game hosts and Tailscale are not the public server's lifecycle.
+Usage: python tools/run/host_server.py --root /projects/mkw-recomp-server --lan-ip ADDRESS --public-ip ADDRESS
+       Add --start to enable the two isolated systemd user services after the binaries have been built.
+"""
+import argparse
+import ipaddress
+from pathlib import Path
+import secrets
+import subprocess
+
+
+def write_private(path: Path, text: str) -> None:
+    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
+    path.write_text(text)
+    path.chmod(0o600)
+
+
+def main() -> None:
+    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.splitlines()[0])
+    ap.add_argument("--root", type=Path, required=True)
+    ap.add_argument("--lan-ip", type=ipaddress.IPv4Address, required=True)
+    ap.add_argument("--public-ip", type=ipaddress.IPv4Address, required=True)
+    ap.add_argument("--port", type=int, default=18443)
+    ap.add_argument("--start", action="store_true")
+    args = ap.parse_args()
+    if not 1024 <= args.port <= 65533:
+        ap.error("port must leave space for the friends API at port + 1")
+    root = args.root.resolve()
+    lobby = root / "build/server/mkw-server"
+    relay = root / "deps/coturn/bin/turnserver"
+    if not lobby.is_file() or not relay.is_file():
+        ap.error("build mkw-server and install coturn under ROOT/deps/coturn first")
+    data = root / "server"
+    data.mkdir(mode=0o700, parents=True, exist_ok=True)
+    data.chmod(0o700)
+    settings = data / "settings.txt"
+    values = dict(line.split("=", 1) for line in settings.read_text().splitlines() if "=" in line) if settings.exists() else {}
+    values.update(turn_host=str(args.public_ip), turn_port="3479")
+    values.setdefault("turn_secret", secrets.token_hex(24))
+    if len(values["turn_secret"]) < 32:
+        ap.error("the existing TURN secret is too short; no service was started")
+    write_private(settings, "".join(f"{key}={value}\n" for key, value in values.items()))
+    config = root / "turnserver.conf"
+    lines = ["# MKW-managed relay", "listening-port=3479", f"listening-ip={args.lan_ip}",
+             f"relay-ip={args.lan_ip}", f"external-ip={args.public_ip}/{args.lan_ip}",
+             "realm=mkw-recomp", "use-auth-secret", f"static-auth-secret={values['turn_secret']}",
+             "min-port=49152", "max-port=49407", "total-quota=128", "user-quota=4", "relay-threads=1",
+             "no-tcp", "no-tcp-relay", "no-tls", "no-multicast-peers", "log-file=stdout"]
+    # The public relay must not provide UDP access to the server's private LAN or local applications.
+    for block in ["0.0.0.0-0.255.255.255", "10.0.0.0-10.255.255.255", "100.64.0.0-100.127.255.255",
+                  "127.0.0.0-127.255.255.255", "169.254.0.0-169.254.255.255", "172.16.0.0-172.31.255.255",
+                  "192.168.0.0-192.168.255.255", "224.0.0.0-255.255.255.255"]:
+        lines.append(f"denied-peer-ip={block}")
+    write_private(config, "\n".join(lines) + "\n")
+    units = Path.home() / ".config/systemd/user"
+    commands = {"mkw-lobby": f"{lobby} --host {args.lan_ip} --port {args.port} --data {data}",
+                "mkw-relay": f"{relay} -c {config}"}
+    for name, command in commands.items():
+        path = units / f"{name}.service"
+        if path.exists() and "# MKW-managed" not in path.read_text():
+            ap.error(f"refusing to replace an unmanaged unit: {path}")
+        write_private(path, f"""# MKW-managed
+[Unit]
+Description=Mario Kart shared {'lobby' if name == 'mkw-lobby' else 'relay'}
+After=network-online.target
+[Service]
+Type=simple
+WorkingDirectory={root}
+ExecStart={command}
+Restart=on-failure
+RestartSec=3
+TimeoutStopSec=10
+UMask=0077
+NoNewPrivileges=yes
+MemoryHigh=128M
+MemoryMax=256M
+CPUQuota=50%
+TasksMax=32
+[Install]
+WantedBy=default.target
+""")
+    if args.start:
+        subprocess.run(["systemctl", "--user", "daemon-reload"], check=True)
+        # enable --now does not reload the config of an already-running service.
+        # Restart both so the new relay settings and server binary are actually used.
+        subprocess.run(["systemctl", "--user", "enable", "mkw-relay.service", "mkw-lobby.service"], check=True)
+        subprocess.run(["systemctl", "--user", "restart", "mkw-relay.service", "mkw-lobby.service"], check=True)
+        subprocess.run(["systemctl", "--user", "is-active", "mkw-relay.service", "mkw-lobby.service"], check=True)
+    print(f"Configured lobby {args.lan_ip}:{args.port}, friends API {args.port + 1}, relay UDP 3479/49152-49407.")
+    print("The shared relay secret remains in owner-only files and was not printed.")
+
+
+if __name__ == "__main__":
+    main()
